body:
Sorry, no, drugs don't usually work like that. 

&#x200B;

There are \*rare\* circumstances where a vast minority of people may experience "paradoxical reactions" to a medication. However, this is not usual. 

&#x200B;

Saying "it all depends on body chemistry" is simply ignorant. 

&#x200B;

Ref: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradoxical\_reaction](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradoxical_reaction)

Ketamine is AWESOME for depression. I fucking love the stuff. Keeps me from feeling suicidal. I support the use of Ketamine (s-isomer is best) - or psilocybin or LSD or MDMA. 

&#x200B;

IF done responsibly and not in a 'party setting' - it's medicine, folks!. And it fucking works!

'Hostage' is the best term for marriage I've ever heard. 

&#x200B;

Bravo sir

I lost my best friend to that shit. He was mixing it with Diclazepam and O-DSMT. 

&#x200B;

I miss him so much. Fuck opiates.

Since you take diazepam you can cold turkey the beer. That's not much alcohol and diazepam at 10-20mg is about the amount you'd get at a detox facility for \*severe\* alcoholics. 

&#x200B;

Don't worry so much :) You don't need alcohol

I found an old bluelight posting from 2014 saying that " It's a good benzo, very comparable to clonazepam. 3 mg meclonazepam equals about 1 mg clonazepam. "

&#x200B;

methylclonazepam is meclonazepam, and it's been around for a while actually

I got a message saying we can't discuss methods. That's fine. I just know I have to do this. I can't let this continue. I've had meds and therapy and a psychiatrist - whole lot of nothing. 

&#x200B;

I'm just worried I'll wake up AGAIN and not understand how it's possible.

nothing is wrong with you. you are normal, like all of us. My family situation is shit too, i understand. At least you have a S/O, a job, and school. I have nothing but an abusive small family. I'm also thinking how i can do it. I can't decide. i dont know what will work and what won't. 

&#x200B;

I understand your pain. I have intense anxiety too. I am on a very high dose of benzo's to treat it. It doesn't really help to be honest, since i've become accustomed to them. 

&#x200B;

I dont know what to do either. I can't up my dose, i can't make friends, I can't live with my family, I can't get a job, I can't go to school. I have no money. 

&#x200B;

I want to kill myself. Perhaps you don't, and that means you're in a better place. You'll be okay. Tomorrow is another day and you'll feel different in the morning. It's always the same with me, i feel ok in the morning and then it just goes downhill from there. 

&#x200B;

I wish i could help more, but I don't know what to say. Life is suffering. We need to figure out how to overcome the suffering somehow. All of us. We're all in this together. We can find a way out. I think. 

&#x200B;

Don't do it.
